# Line endings are part of the contract for two things here: `SKILL.md` is parsed as YAML by the
# host (a CRLF fence is not `---\n`), and `scripts/*.sh` is executed by bash (a CRLF shebang is not
# a shebang). Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true turns 6 green tests red —
# which reads as a broken product, not a broken checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
